Grayswandir is silver, so it does an extra d20 against silver haters, which
are  V's, Werefoos, and all (except the riders?) &'s, shades, and maybe some
other things I'm forgetting.  It does double damage against all enemies as
well (the d20 isn't doubled)

As far as level drain resistance, I've never seen it as a problem, for a
couple of reasons:

-Most level draining monsters are fairly weak, so they die quickly.  The
toughest (IIRC) are V's, but V's get destroyed by silver, so they aren't a
problem.

-Magic cancellation of 3 (most good cloaks have MC3) pretty much blocks
level draining, reducing it's chance of effectiveness to less than 2% (plus,
the attack has to beat your AC, IIRC)

-Most combat type characters don't really want to be high level anyway, so
losing a level isn't so bad.  Spellcasters might care more, but again, the
odds of the draining succeeding are pretty low

-Finally, when you get level drained, you are like 1 exp away from getting
that level back, so once you kill the attacker you're pretty much where you
started (barring the randomness of hp/mp growth)


Also, Grayswandir gives the unique ability to resist hallucinations while
you're wielding it.

So, in my opinion (based on my experiences) A Grayswandir beats out an
Excalibur any day.  Excalibur is fairly easy to get and is handy for early
game problems (I like auto searching), but given the choice between the two,
I'd use a Grayswandir.


